ation about\nhealth impacts and how ozone pollution forms in Colorado, visit:\nhttps://cdphe.colorado.gov/ozone- pollution-and-your-health\n\nHEALTH INFORMATION...Increasing likelihood of respiratory symptoms\nand breathing discomfort in active children and adults and people\nwith lung disease, such as asthma. Active children and adults, and\npeople with lung disease, such as asthma, should reduce prolonged\nor heavy outdoor exertion.","ends":"2026-08-18T16:00:00-06:00","severity":"Unknown","areaDesc":"Broomfield, CO; Adams, CO; Larimer, CO; Jefferson, CO; Denver, CO; Boulder, CO; Weld, CO; Arapahoe, CO; Douglas, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.29db7d75e717a3fee3b2dbc6474566b8c1f30705.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.29db7d75e717a3fee3b2dbc6474566b8c1f30705.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-08-17T23:22:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KBOU 172322 AFDBOU Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Denver/Boulder CO 522 PM MDT Mon Aug 17 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Warmer on Tuesday, with isolated to scattered showers and thunderstorms. - More active weather day shaping up for Wednesday with scattered severe thunderstorm threat. - Warmer again through the coming weekend with above normal temperatures. Drier Thursday ","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=BOU&issuedby=BOU&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-08-17T19:29:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION...Rest of today through Tuesday...Warmer and drier conditions are forecast today with light winds. Relative humidity values are expected to drop to around 15-25% across most of the high country and I-25 corridor. A couple of showers or thunderstorms are possible across the plains this afternoon though wetting rain chances are low. A weak cold front is expected to move through the lower","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=BOU&issuedby=BOU&product=FWF&format=CI"},"coagmet":{"station_id":"ftl01","station_nam